    GROUP /entry/instrument/lockin_amplifier [NXlockin]  (14 members)
      Concept   : NXsts/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier  [RECOMMENDED]
      Inheritance:
        NXsts/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier
          Doc       : The lock-in amplifier information.
        NXspm/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier
          Doc       : The lock-in amplifier information.
        NXlockin
          Doc       : A base class definition for a lock-in amplifier. The lock-in amplifier
                      information: the device is being used to extract a (potentially) very weak
                      input signal buried in the noisy background, where the input signal has the
                      same frequency (or its harmonic) as carrier signal or reference signal, using
                      heterodyne detection. This method extracts the amplitude and phase shift
                      between input signal and reference signal. In single phase lock-in amplifiers
                      used in high signal-to-noise ratio applications, only the amplitude is
                      measured and phase difference is set to zero. In two phase lock-in amplifiers
                      used in low signal-to-noise ratio applications, both the amplitude and phase
                      difference are measured. Fields with partial names like low_passN, high_passN,
                      etc., can be repeated for each channel of the lockin amplifier. It is
                      envisioned that these fields are named low_pass_0, low_pass_1, and so on.
      FIELD /entry/instrument/lockin_amplifier/demodulated_signal  shape=()  dtype=object
        Value     : current
        Concept   : NXlockin/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier/demodulated_signal  [OPTIONAL]
        Inheritance:
          NXlockin/demodulated_signal
            Doc       : Type of the demodulated signal, current | voltage | bias. The name of the
                        current or voltage signal can be also specified according to their purpose
                        (e.g., `bias` voltage).
        Enums     : [NXlockin] current, voltage, bias
        Enums     : [NXlockin] current, voltage, bias
      FIELD /entry/instrument/lockin_amplifier/flip_sign  shape=()  dtype=float64
        Value     : -1.0
        Concept   : NXspm/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier/flip_sign  [OPTIONAL]
        Inheritance:
          NXspm/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier/flip_sign
            Doc       : The sign (1 or -1) that renders the values of the lock-in current positive.
                        The calibration procedure with retracted tip is normally performed to
                        compensate for the signal phase delay in SPM. The procedure yields two
                        possible solutions corresponding to the chosen phase, this number should be
                        equal to 1 or -1 depending on which solution is chosen (this concept mainly
                        used in STS experiments).
      FIELD /entry/instrument/lockin_amplifier/harmonic_order_d1  shape=()  dtype=int64
        Value     : 1
        Concept   : NXlockin/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/lockin_amplifier/harmonic_orderN  [OPTIONAL]
        Inheritance:
          NXlockin/harmonic_orderN
            Doc       : The reference signal can be a higher harmonic of the modulation signal. Here
                        the order of the harmonic is stored. N is envisioned to represent the
                        channel number e.g., harmonic_order1.
