            FIELD /entry/instrument/piezo_sensor/piezo_configuration/calibration/calibration_parameters/second_order_correction_x  shape=()  dtype=float64
              Value     : 0.0
              Concept   : NXspm_piezo_config/ENTRY/INSTRUMENT/piezo_sensor/piezo_configuration/calibration/calibration_parameters/second_order_correctionN  [OPTIONAL]
              Inheritance:
                NXspm_piezo_config/calibration/calibration_parameters/second_order_correctionN
                  Doc       : The N (substring) denotes X and Y directions (e.g.,
                              second_order_correction_x). If you know them, you can enter the 2nd
                              order piezo characteristics to compensate the error for that axis. The
                              following equation shows the interpretation of the 2nd order
                              correction parameters, For the X-piezo: :math:`U_x = \frac{1}{c_x}
                              \cdot X + c_{xx} \cdot X^2` with units: :math:`[V] = \frac{[V]}{[m]}
                              \cdot [m] + \frac{[V]}{[m^2]} \cdot [m^2]` where cx is the calibration
                              of the piezo X and cxx is the 2nd order correction. The unit for the
                              second-order correction is (:math:`\frac{V}{m^2}`).
                NXparameters/PARAMETER
                  Doc       : A parameter that is used in or results from processing.
              @units = V / m ** 2  [OPTIONAL]
            FIELD /entry/instrument/piezo_sensor/piezo_configuration/calibration/calibration_parameters/second_order_correction_y  shape=()  dtype=float64
              Value     : 0.0
